---
description: Keep every Breditor action and primitive operation isolated, documented, and auditable
alwaysApply: true
---

# Action and operation modules

- Put every semantic action in its own lower-snake-case file under `src/action/`.
- Put every primitive operation in its own lower-snake-case file under `src/operation/`.
- Match the filename to the primary Rust type: `InsertText` belongs in
  `action/insert_text.rs`; `TextSplice` belongs in `operation/text_splice.rs`.
- Keep `mod.rs` limited to declarations, a closed routing enum when needed, and
  curated re-exports. It must contain no action or operation semantics.
- Actions plan standard operations; they never mutate document nodes directly.
- Do not create an action before its required operation and relocation laws exist.

Every action file must document its stable ID/version, payload validation,
structural preconditions, planned operations, selection and pending-format
behavior, history boundaries, stale/replay behavior, structured failures, and
representative laws/tests.

Every operation file must own its checked apply behavior, canonical applied
record, actual inverse, relocation, coalescing rule, encoding, and property tests.

Do not add catch-all `types.rs`, `utils.rs`, `helpers.rs`, or `misc.rs` files.
